WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.343
Scenario: You are working in a shared café. Your

2
00:00:03.343 --> 00:00:06.686
laptop is unlocked while you step away, a sensitive

3
00:00:06.686 --> 00:00:10.400
dashboard is visible, and you are connected to public Wi-Fi.

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.743
Safest response: Option B: Lock the device before stepping

5
00:00:13.743 --> 00:00:17.086
away, keep it physically controlled, use a trusted connection

6
00:00:17.086 --> 00:00:20.429
and follow remote-access policy. Physical access, screen exposure and

7
00:00:20.429 --> 00:00:23.771
network risks require layered controls. Option A is unsafe

8
00:00:23.771 --> 00:00:27.114
because Minimizing a window does not protect the unattended

9
00:00:27.114 --> 00:00:30.457
device or session. Option C is unsafe because Removing

10
00:00:30.457 --> 00:00:33.800
automatic locking increases the opportunity for unauthorized access. Option

11
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.143
D is unsafe because An unknown bystander is not

12
00:00:37.143 --> 00:00:40.486
an appropriate security control. In practice: Lock the screen

13
00:00:40.486 --> 00:00:43.829
whenever unattended, keep devices in your control, avoid exposing

14
00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:47.171
sensitive content and use the approved secure connection method.

15
00:00:47.171 --> 00:00:50.514
Key takeaway: Remote work combines physical, visual and network

16
00:00:50.514 --> 00:00:52.000
risks; use layered protection.
